.Dt LIBNETWORKCMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm networkcmp_hello ,
.Nm networkcmp_connect ,
.Nm networkcmp_connect_ex ,
.Nm networkcmp_udp ,
.Nm networkcmp_resolve ,
.Nm networkcmp_getaddrinfo ,
.Nm networkcmp_freeaddrinfo ,
.Nm networkcmp_client_open ,
.Nm networkcmp_client_limits ,
.Nm networkcmp_client_close
.Nd public client for the system network broker
.Sh LIBRARY
.Li libnetworkcmp
.Pq Fl lnetworkcmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In networkcmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn networkcmp_client_open "struct networkcmp_client **client"
.Ft "const struct networkcmp_hello_reply *"
.Fn networkcmp_client_limits "const struct networkcmp_client *client"
.Ft void
.Fn networkcmp_client_close "struct networkcmp_client *client"
.Ft int
.Fn networkcmp_hello "struct networkcmp_client *client" "struct networkcmp_hello_reply *reply"
.Ft int
.Fn networkcmp_connect "struct networkcmp_client *client" "const struct sockaddr *address" "socklen_t address_length" "int *out_fd"
.Ft int
.Fn networkcmp_connect_ex "struct networkcmp_client *client" "const struct sockaddr *address" "socklen_t address_length" "uint32_t timeout_ms" "int *out_fd"
.Ft int
.Fn networkcmp_udp "struct networkcmp_client *client" "const struct sockaddr *peer" "socklen_t peer_length" "int *out_fd"
.Ft int
.Fn networkcmp_resolve "struct networkcmp_client *client" "const char *host" "const char *service" "uint32_t family" "uint32_t socket_type" "uint32_t flags" "struct networkcmp_resolve_result *results" "size_t *nresults" "char *canonname" "size_t canonname_size" "uint32_t *ttl_seconds"
.Ft int
.Fn networkcmp_getaddrinfo "struct networkcmp_client *client" "const char *host" "const char *service" "const struct addrinfo *hints" "struct addrinfo **result"
.Ft void
.Fn networkcmp_freeaddrinfo "struct addrinfo *result"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library is the client for the version
.Dv 1.0.0
.Dv system.Network
system network broker.
The broker follows the Casper model: it performs DNS and socket operations
under an immutable, session-derived policy and returns
.Em real, connected, rights-limited socket descriptors .
It never proxies application data and exposes no emulated socket handle.
The caller owns all I/O on the returned descriptor.
.Pp
The
.Fn networkcmp_client_open
function consumes the local broker session channel that
.Xr serviced 8
injects.
The library creates one process-wide, token-correlated session, performs the
initial negotiation with
.Fn networkcmp_hello ,
and records the negotiated values; repeated opens return references to that
same authority.
The reply returned by
.Fn networkcmp_client_limits
is the binding contract for the protocol version, features, and the resolve
result bound.
There is no global lookup or fallback path.
.Pp
.Fn networkcmp_connect
policy-checks the destination
.Fa address ,
opens and connects a TCP socket to it, and stores the connected descriptor in
.Fa out_fd .
.Fn networkcmp_udp
opens a datagram socket, connects it to
.Fa peer ,
and returns that descriptor; a connected UDP socket exchanges datagrams only
with its peer.
Both accept an
.Vt AF_INET
or
.Vt AF_INET6
.Vt sockaddr .
The returned descriptor is delivered out of band over the session channel with
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS
and is limited before delivery to only the rights a data path needs:
.Dv CAP_READ ,
.Dv CAP_WRITE ,
.Dv CAP_EVENT ,
.Dv CAP_SHUTDOWN ,
.Dv CAP_GETSOCKOPT ,
.Dv CAP_SETSOCKOPT ,
.Dv CAP_FCNTL
.Pq Dv F_GETFL and Dv F_SETFL for Dv O_NONBLOCK ,
.Dv CAP_FSTAT ,
and
.Dv CAP_IOCTL
restricted to
.Dv FIONREAD , FIONBIO ,
and
.Dv FIOASYNC .
It cannot bind, connect, listen, accept, or be transferred again.
A denied or failed request returns
.Li -1 ,
sets
.Va errno
to the broker's connect status, and leaves
.Fa out_fd
set to
.Li -1 .
.Pp
.Fn networkcmp_connect_ex
is
.Fn networkcmp_connect
with a client-supplied handshake deadline
.Fa timeout_ms
in milliseconds: the broker connects non-blocking and, if the TCP handshake does
not complete within the deadline, fails the request with
.Er ETIMEDOUT
and delivers no descriptor.
A
.Fa timeout_ms
of zero is identical to
.Fn networkcmp_connect
.Pq a fully blocking connect with the kernel default timeout .
.Pp
.Fn networkcmp_resolve
implements bounded
.Xr getaddrinfo 3 Ns -style
forward resolution without exposing provider or resolver descriptors.
The caller supplies the result-array capacity through
.Fa nresults ;
on success it contains the number returned.
An optional canonical-name buffer and TTL output may be supplied; a TTL of
zero means the provider does not expose TTL information.
The broker resolves independently of its request loop and permits one active
resolution per session; an overlapping resolution fails with
.Er EBUSY .
.Fn networkcmp_getaddrinfo
is the familiar convenience interface.
It translates the bounded results into a linked
.Vt struct addrinfo
list and returns an
.Dv EAI_*
status.
The resulting list must be released with
.Fn networkcmp_freeaddrinfo ,
not
.Xr freeaddrinfo 3 .
The
.Fa hints Ns 's
.Va ai_flags
may combine
.Dv AI_PASSIVE , AI_CANONNAME , AI_NUMERICHOST , AI_NUMERICSERV ,
.Dv AI_ADDRCONFIG , AI_V4MAPPED ,
and
.Dv AI_ALL ;
any other flag fails with
.Dv EAI_BADFLAGS .
.Dv AI_ADDRCONFIG
is accepted for source compatibility but is a documented no-op in the in-process
resolver.
.Dv AI_V4MAPPED
and
.Dv AI_ALL
are honored: an
.Vt AF_INET6
resolve may return IPv4-mapped IPv6 results, and with
.Dv AI_ALL
both native
.Dv AAAA
and mapped
.Dv A
results are returned.
.Pp
Kernel channel reply tokens correlate concurrent calls so threads cannot
consume one another's replies.
The opaque client is process-bound.
The injected broker session is retained as process-lifetime authority;
.Fn networkcmp_client_close
releases a library borrow, and a later
.Fn networkcmp_client_open
reacquires the same managed session without creating another channel reader.
If the broker returns a malformed reply, the library marks this authority
terminal: the failing operation and every later operation return
.Er EPROTO
without sending another request.
After
.Xr fork 2 ,
the child cannot reuse the parent's session and must open a separately
injected authority if one exists.
.Pp
Version 1 provides only DNS resolution and connected TCP and UDP sockets.
Listeners are declared through
.Fn activation.socket
and are not created through this client API.
Protocol space for future userspace networking is reserved but implemented as
none; any such behavior requires a separately negotiated protocol version.
.Pp
The
.Ql networkcmp
DTrace provider exposes component-open, message-send, message-receive, and
message-reject probes.
Provider daemons audit policy decisions through OpenBSM; client-library
activity is operational telemetry and is not audited.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_net 3 ,
.Xr getaddrinfo 3 ,
.Xr libchannel 3 ,
.Xr libservice 3
